@startuml migration-activity
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
title Moving an old profile: start-up's step 4 (migrate.rs)

start
:**M0. Detect** (reads only); <<#DDEBF7>>
if (data/layout.json, the marker, is there?) then (yes)
  if (written by a newer F1R3Gaze?) then (yes)
    :the session only reads; <<#F8CBAD>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :**M9** if a migration's folder is left:
    remove its plan, then the folder; <<#FCE4D6>>
    stop
  endif
elseif (data/.migration/plan.json is there?) then (yes: resume)
  :read the plan: the same actions
  and the same backup session; <<#DDEBF7>>
elseif (an old profile with a signature file?) then (yes)
  :**M1. Plan** every action, read only,
  then write plan.json with write_new; <<#FCE4D6>>
else (no: a new profile)
  :create the marker with write_new; <<#FCE4D6>>
  stop
endif
:**M2.** create every folder the moves need,
each synced in its parent; <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M3.** write each converted file
(settings.toml, session.json, history.json)
with write_new: never replacing anything; <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M4.** move each item: link the new name and sync,
then unlink the old one and sync
(across file systems: copy, sync, read back, compare); <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M5.** move each converted original into
<class>/backups/<session>/legacy-profile/; <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M6.** rename each cache shard into cache/content/,
synced in both folders
(left behind on another file system); <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M6b.** remove the old folders the moves emptied
(keys/, exports/, store/, logs/, cache/): only an empty
folder can go. M7's write syncs the old folder; <<#DDEBF7>>
:**M7.** write MIGRATED.txt into the old folder; <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M8.** create the marker; <<#FCE4D6>>
:**M9.** remove the plan, then its folder; <<#FCE4D6>>
stop

note right
  **Something already at a destination**: a conflict.
  Both are kept, and MIGRATED.txt names it.
  **A step that fails** (M2 to M5): the session only reads,
  and the next start resumes the plan; finished steps
  are then no-ops.
  **A crash at any step**: the next start runs the barrier
  (there is no marker yet), then resumes the plan.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze code, reading |
  |<#FCE4D6> | a durable write |
  |<#F8CBAD> | the session only reads |
endlegend
@enduml
